From 3fec094bb37f5dd0dbea6f05cd29532f6de85999 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:58:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 071/122] Object map: no empty chunk when the last object
 closes one

When the last handle filled a chunk of the object map (over 2030 bytes),
the 2 bytes reserved for the next chunk stayed as zeros before the final
chunk of size 2; ACadSharp read past the end. Hit by sample_AC1032 as
R2000 after bit_write_UMC got shorter.

* src/encode.c (encode_objects_handles): Drop the reserved size then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/encode.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/encode.c b/src/encode.c
index eaa73c4..6481333 100644
--- a/src/encode.c
+++ b/src/encode.c
@@ -3344,6 +3344,10 @@ encode_objects_handles (Dwg_Data *restrict dwg, Bit_Chain *restrict dat,
 #endif
       bit_write_CRC_BE (dat, size_adr, 0xC0C1);
     }
+  else
+    // the last object closed a chunk: drop the size reserved for the next,
+    // else 2 zero bytes stood before the last chunk of size 2
+    dat->byte -= 2;
 #ifndef NDEBUG
   if (dwg->header.version >= R_1_2 && dwg->header.version < R_2004)
     {
-- 
2.43.0

